A||||4||ig88vsbobafett||Ok V6 in a 84 ?? How can it be done easly  or 120hp out of a duke||||1||
Z||000000||ig88vsbobafett||12-30-2001||11:25 PM||||Would a Carbed 2.8 go in it with out having to do to much rewiring ???<BR>It is a 2.5 right now or would any one know what do do to get 120HP out of a 2.5 ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Hairy_Fiero||12-31-2001||12:06 AM||||Head work, holley TBI, cold air intake and get rid of the cat with a straight pipe if possible. That should get you around there. Or you could do a mild turbo at 4-5 psi for pretty cheap. Hard part would be the exhaust work and bracket to mount it properly. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jake_Dragon||12-31-2001||07:06 AM||||Wish you had a V8.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||avengador1||12-31-2001||08:52 AM||||You can do plenty of work on the duke to get more h.p. all you have to do is to increase your volumetric efficiency. Remember the engine is just a pump, if you can move more air thru it you will make more horsepower. The easiest modifications are to the intake and exhaust. Change out your restrictive air filter for an intake tube with a K&N filter or just get a K&N filter to fit your filter housing. You can change the factory exhaust manifolds for headers. A good set of balanced headers will give you a decent increase in horse power. You could also have your cylinder head ported and polished and get a 3 angle valve job. As I understand the stock block cannot handle any amount of boost pressure, like a super charger or turbo. You can have the whole engine balanced and blueprinted. This will let you rev it up higher and faster without it blowing up. I would stick to the simpler mods first. If your not happy with the results you could go as big as a V8 if you want or your budget allows. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||88CoupeV6||12-31-2001||09:30 AM||||I am going to do a v6 or 88 duke on jaygee79's 84 SE this summer. <P>The best way to do it is to get a complete wire harness from an 86-88 fiero and re run the entire car. Also you have to run the fuel lines from a 86-88 fiero as they run on the right side. <P>Josh<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||1
